From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:17:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 104/342] kernel: build without KDEBUG on arm64; a signal frame
 bug it hid

arch_setup_signal_frame() read the commpage's signal handler address
inside ASSERT(): without KDEBUG the read was compiled out, and every
signal handler would have been entered at an uninitialized address.
Read it, then check the result.

Two build failures without KDEBUG: arch_int_gicv3.cpp relied on cpu.h
and interrupts.h coming in through debug headers; dec_vnode_ref_count()
returns B_BAD_VALUE for a NULL vnode, since AutoLocker accepts NULL and
GCC otherwise warns of a NULL reaching atomic_add().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int_gicv3.cpp | 2 ++
 src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_thread.cpp    | 7 +++++--
 src/system/kernel/fs/vfs.cpp                    | 5 +++++
 3 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int_gicv3.cpp b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int_gicv3.cpp
index d067512798..bb32e0d2d6 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int_gicv3.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_int_gicv3.cpp
@@ -6,8 +6,10 @@
 
 #include "arch_int_gicv3.h"
 
+#include "cpu.h"
 #include "debug.h"
 #include "gicv3_regs.h"
+#include "interrupts.h"
 #include "smp.h"
 #include "vm/vm.h"
 
diff --git a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_thread.cpp b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_thread.cpp
index a3f60bcacf..263c74cf36 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_thread.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/arch/arm64/arch_thread.cpp
@@ -201,9 +201,12 @@ arch_setup_signal_frame(Thread *thread, struct sigaction *sa,
 
 	addr_t commpageAddr = (addr_t)thread->team->commpage_address;
 	addr_t signalHandlerAddr;
-	ASSERT(user_memcpy(&signalHandlerAddr,
+	// not inside ASSERT(): without KDEBUG it would not be read at all
+	res = user_memcpy(&signalHandlerAddr,
 		&((addr_t*)commpageAddr)[COMMPAGE_ENTRY_ARM64_SIGNAL_HANDLER],
-		sizeof(signalHandlerAddr)) >= B_OK);
+		sizeof(signalHandlerAddr));
+	if (res < B_OK)
+		return res;
 	signalHandlerAddr += commpageAddr;
 
 	frame->lr = frame->elr;
diff --git a/src/system/kernel/fs/vfs.cpp b/src/system/kernel/fs/vfs.cpp
index e155fa895e..ac36768e00 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/fs/vfs.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/fs/vfs.cpp
@@ -1062,6 +1062,11 @@ free_vnode(struct vnode* vnode, bool reenter)
 static status_t
 dec_vnode_ref_count(struct vnode* vnode, bool alwaysFree, bool reenter)
 {
+	// AutoLocker accepts NULL; without KDEBUG's checks GCC then sees a NULL
+	// vnode reaching atomic_add() (-Wstringop-overflow)
+	if (vnode == NULL)
+		return B_BAD_VALUE;
+
 	ReadLocker locker(sVnodeLock);
 	AutoLocker<Vnode> nodeLocker(vnode);
 
